<description>
Complete every partial centered motif using the complete motifs visible in the same grid.

Input structure:
- The background contains one or more complete 3x3 motifs, each with a center color and a symmetric same-color shell mask.
- Other copies of those motifs are partial: either the center pixel is present without its shell, or the shell is present without its center.
- For each center color, the complete motif uniquely determines the shell color and shell offsets.

Rule:
- Infer every complete motif as center color -> (shell color, shell offsets).
- Around every pixel with a known center color, fill missing shell-offset background pixels with the shell color.
- At every background pixel whose surrounding offsets already contain a complete shell, fill the center with that motif's center color.

Key insight:
The complete motifs are templates that make center-only and shell-only partial copies two views of the same local sprite.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "complete centered 3x3 motif template s with center color, shell color, and symmetric shell offsets",
  "dst": "partial motif copy d: either a center pixel alone or a matching shell mask around an empty center",
  "match_cond": "d.center_color == s.center_color, or d.shell_color == s.shell_color and d.shell_offsets == s.shell_offsets",
  "transform": "paint d's missing shell pixels or missing center pixel to complete the matched motif"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-19 rows x 12-22 cols, background 0
  templates:
    count: 1-3 distinct motif types per grid
    shape: centered 3x3 motif; symmetric offset mask chosen from {horizontal-bar, vertical-bar, plus, X-corners}
    colors: each template has a unique center_color and shell_color; center and shell color sets are disjoint
    size: 3 pixels (bar shapes) or 5 pixels (plus/X shapes)
    constraint: all templates in one grid have distinct offset shapes [observed]
  partials:
    per_template: 1-3 partial copies (center-only or shell-only)
    center_only: just the center pixel placed alone (shell pixels are bg)
    shell_only: just the shell pixels placed (center pixel is bg); 0-2 per grid total
    total_partials: 3-7 across all templates
  placement:
    all completed motifs (template + partials after fill) must fit in-bounds
    no two completed motifs overlap or touch (Chebyshev gap >= 2 between bboxes)
    partials are scattered far from their template (Manhattan >= 7)
  output_rule: |
    For each center-only partial, paint the missing shell pixels around the center.
    For each shell-only partial, paint the missing center pixel inside the shell.
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims in [13-19] x [12-22], and 1-3 template shapes (distinct from {h-bar, v-bar, plus, X}).
    2. Assign each template a unique (center_color, shell_color) pair from non-zero colors; center and shell sets disjoint.
    3. For each template, decide 1-3 partial copies (mix of center-only and shell-only; at least 1 shell-only across all templates).
    4. Place all completed motifs (1 template + its partials) on the grid with Chebyshev bbox gap >= 2. Each motif center must allow full shape in-bounds (margin >= 1).
    5. Record the output grid (all motifs complete).
    6. Derive input by removing shell pixels from center-only partials and removing center pixel from shell-only partials. Templates stay complete.
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

